comment = "Nested virtualization test harness and measurement store"

desc = <<EOD
The test harness for nested virtualization: the boot and guest-lifecycle
tests, the hardware and parity probes, the soak and stress drivers, and the
SQLite measurement store that keeps every figure alongside the build it was
taken on.

Run the suite with:

	kyua test -k /usr/tests/sys/vmm/nested/Kyuafile

That needs kyua and atf-sh, which arrive with any FreeBSD system's test suite
and are already present on a machine that has one. This package does not depend
on them, because doing so would name the CloudBSD copies, and those replace
files an installed FreeBSD test suite already owns. The harness is packaged
apart from the rest of the test suite so that it can be added to a machine that
keeps its existing userland, which is what a dependency on the CloudBSD test
suite would prevent.

The measurement store is SQLite, reached through python3 and its sqlite3
module, which FreeBSD ships as a version-specific package -- py312-sqlite3 on a
3.12 host. Neither is a dependency of this package, because the tests and the
harness run without them; only the store needs them, and it says so plainly when
the import fails rather than recording nothing.

It also does not depend on the nested virtualization kernel. Measuring a stock
kernel is how a baseline is taken, and a dependency would make the harness
uninstallable in exactly the boot environment where that baseline is measured.
EOD

annotations {
	set = nested
}
